{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310810,"nonce":"TxdYpYXlX0BOMCw9RmoqvSQSF6Y=","title":"MEASURED NET LOSS: narrowing the Q4_K dot's scales/accumulator from Float(f64) to Single(f32) is ~5% SLOWER prefill on x86, 4/4 pairwise, ...","message":"`Single` (f32) shipped so the k-quant dot could use f32 scales like llama.cpp.\nThe arm is a 3-line change to `nue/nue/Q4Matmul.hx` (staged as `~/q4_f32.hx`\non the NUC, baseline `~/q4_base.hx`, harness `~/bench_kernel.sh \u003carm\u003e \u003crun\u003e`):\n\n    f16ToF32(bits:Int):Float            -\u003e :Single\n    q4DotMA4(..., xd:Float):Float       -\u003e xd:Single):Single\n    subDot(..., xd/d/dmin: Float)       -\u003e Single\n\n\n| pair | base ttft | f32 ttft | delta |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 | 12.043 | 12.634 | +4.9% |\n| 1 | 12.042 | 12.938 | +7.4% |\n| 2 | 13.041 | 13.679 | +4.9% |\n| 3 | 12.716 | 13.260 | +4.3% |\n\n**4/4 pairwise SLOWER on prefill, median ~+4.9%.** Decode also never better\n(base 38.5-42.8 tok/s vs f32 38.3-39.9, 4/4). Output stays COHERENT but\nDIVERGES in wording — narrowing the accumulator changes the logits, so this is\nnot a bit-identical swap even at temp=0. Tree restored to base.\n\nScalar f64 and f32 have the same latency on x86; narrowing buys no arithmetic\nspeed. The dot's heavy lifting is already VNNI integer work, so the scales are\na small term — and `Single` is `to Float from Float`, so every boundary with a\nFloat local inserts a conversion. Net: same math, extra converts.\n\n**This does NOT indict `Single`.** The type is correct and shipped\n([[feature_single_f32_scalar]]); enabling it also forced out a real\nheap-corruption bug ([[bugs_stdtypes_type_addition_breaks_nue]]). It is *this\napplication* — narrowing an already-integer-dominated dot — that is a wash.\n\nUnchanged: the gap is STRUCTURAL, not arithmetic precision. In order —\n**2-D blocking first** ([[perf_repack_confirmed_x86_prefill_but_not_first]]:\n2/3 of the gap is kernel structure, 2.67x), then weight repack (+41.5%\nmeasured). Disassembly says 52% of the kernel is scalar ADDRESS ARITHMETIC\n([[perf_prefill_gap_is_address_arithmetic]]) — that is the term to attack, not\nthe scale type.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `perf_single_f32_q4_dot_no_win` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}